From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: defcom5-rockchip <defcom5rockchip@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:43:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3588s-orangepi-5: route ES8388 MCLK
 to the IO pin

Fork override of Armbian's patch/kernel/archive/rockchip64-7.3/board-orangepi-5-es8388-route-mclk-to-io.patch.
Armbian's copy (main 978a64cd8, 2026-09-01) has its hunk indented with spaces while the
upstream .dtsi uses tabs, so it fails to apply and Armbian's patcher treats that as fatal,
which stops the NanoPi Zero2 kernel build even though this Orange Pi audio change is
irrelevant to it. Same content, tabs restored. Drop this file once Armbian fixes theirs.

Point the es8388 node's "clocks" at I2S1_8CH_MCLKOUT_TO_IO so the codec driver
enables the MCLK-to-IO gate at probe; "assigned-clocks" stays on I2S1_8CH_MCLKOUT.

Signed-off-by: defcom5-rockchip <defcom5rockchip@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-5b.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-5b.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-5b.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-5b.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5-5b.dtsi
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ &i2c6 {
 	es8388: audio-codec@10 {
 		compatible = "everest,es8388", "everest,es8328";
 		reg = <0x10>;
-		clocks = <&cru I2S1_8CH_MCLKOUT>;
+		clocks = <&cru I2S1_8CH_MCLKOUT_TO_IO>;
 		AVDD-supply = <&vcca_3v3_s0>;
 		DVDD-supply = <&vcca_1v8_s0>;
 		HPVDD-supply = <&vcca_3v3_s0>;
-- 
Armbian
